Feature: Compound Drug Analysis Aggregation and Potential Categorization

  This feature performs compound screening analysis on the purgo_playground.compound_drug_analysis table, including filtering, aggregation, joining, and categorization of results based on overall_score.

  Background:
    Given the source table is "purgo_playground.compound_drug_analysis"
    And the table contains columns: study_id, compound_id, mutation_id, therapeutic_area, drug_name, ic50, auc, efficacy, toxicity, potency, sample_size, mutation_frequency, mutation_severity, compound_concentration, cell_viability, growth_inhibition, result, approved_flag, validation_status, status, created_by, score1, score2, score3, score4, score5
    And only rows where approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid" are included in the analysis
    And null values in ic50, auc, efficacy, score1, score2, score3, score4, score5 are excluded from calculations
    And grouping and joining are performed on therapeutic_area
    And overall_score is calculated as the average of non-null score1, score2, score3, score4, score5 for each row
    And result categorization is as follows:
      | overall_score range | potential_category   |
      | 70 <= score <= 100 | High Potential      |
      | 60 <= score < 70   | Moderate Potential  |
      | score < 60         | Low Potential       |
    And duplicate or missing therapeutic_area values are excluded from grouping and joining
    And join type for Join Analysis is inner join on therapeutic_area
    And the final output displays all columns from compound_drug_analysis plus aggregated columns and result analysis

  Scenario: Happy Path - Aggregation and Categorization for Valid Approved Compounds
    Given the table contains rows with approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    And all required columns (ic50, auc, efficacy, score1, score2, score3, score4, score5, therapeutic_area) are non-null
    When the data is grouped by therapeutic_area
    Then calculate average_ic50 as the mean of ic50 per therapeutic_area
    And calculate average_auc as the mean of auc per therapeutic_area
    And calculate average_efficacy as the mean of efficacy per therapeutic_area
    And calculate total_sample_size as the sum of sample_size per therapeutic_area
    And calculate study_count as the count of distinct study_id per therapeutic_area
    And join the filtered data with aggregated data on therapeutic_area using inner join
    And for each row, calculate overall_score as the average of score1, score2, score3, score4, score5 (ignoring nulls)
    And categorize each row as:
      | overall_score >= 70 and <= 100 | High Potential      |
      | overall_score >= 60 and < 70   | Moderate Potential  |
      | overall_score < 60             | Low Potential       |
    And display all columns from compound_drug_analysis plus average_ic50, average_auc, average_efficacy, total_sample_size, study_count, overall_score, potential_category

  Scenario Outline: Error - Missing Required Values
    Given a row with <missing_column> as null
    When the row is processed for aggregation or overall_score calculation
    Then exclude the row from all calculations and output

    Examples:
      | missing_column |
      | ic50          |
      | auc           |
      | efficacy      |
      | score1        |
      | score2        |
      | score3        |
      | score4        |
      | score5        |
      | therapeutic_area |

  Scenario: Error - Invalid Approved Flag or Validation Status
    Given a row with approved_flag != 1 or validation_status != "valid"
    When the row is processed
    Then exclude the row from all calculations and output

  Scenario: Error - Duplicate or Missing Therapeutic Area
    Given a row with therapeutic_area as null or duplicate
    When the data is grouped or joined on therapeutic_area
    Then exclude rows with null therapeutic_area from all calculations and output
    And group only on unique therapeutic_area values

  Scenario Outline: Data Type Validation for Filtering
    Given a row with approved_flag as <approved_flag_type>
    And validation_status as <validation_status_type>
    When filtering for approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    Then include the row only if approved_flag is integer 1 and validation_status is string "valid"
    And exclude the row otherwise

    Examples:
      | approved_flag_type | validation_status_type |
      | integer            | string                |
      | string             | string                |
      | integer            | integer               |
      | string             | integer               |

  Scenario: Join Analysis - Inner Join on Therapeutic Area
    Given filtered compound_drug_analysis data
    And aggregated data grouped by therapeutic_area
    When performing join analysis
    Then perform an inner join on therapeutic_area
    And retain only rows with matching therapeutic_area in both datasets

  Scenario: Final Output - Display All Columns and Result Analysis
    Given the joined and categorized data
    When generating the final output
    Then display all columns from compound_drug_analysis
    And display aggregated columns: average_ic50, average_auc, average_efficacy, total_sample_size, study_count
    And display result analysis columns: overall_score, potential_category

  Scenario Outline: Potential Category Assignment
    Given a row with overall_score = <overall_score>
    When categorizing potential
    Then assign potential_category as <potential_category>

    Examples:
      | overall_score | potential_category   |
      | 85            | High Potential      |
      | 70            | High Potential      |
      | 69.9          | Moderate Potential  |
      | 60            | Moderate Potential  |
      | 59.9          | Low Potential       |
      | 0             | Low Potential       |

  Scenario: Error - No Matching Therapeutic Area in Join
    Given a row in filtered data with therapeutic_area not present in aggregated data
    When performing inner join
    Then exclude the row from the final output

  Scenario: Error - All Scores Null for a Row
    Given a row where all score1, score2, score3, score4, score5 are null
    When calculating overall_score
    Then exclude the row from categorization and output

  Scenario: Error - Aggregation Level Ambiguity
    Given ambiguity in whether to aggregate at study, compound, or therapeutic_area level
    When performing aggregation
    Then aggregate only at therapeutic_area level as per requirements

  Scenario: Error - Output Destination Not Specified
    Given the output destination is not specified
    When generating the final output
    Then display the results in the notebook and do not write to a new table

  Scenario: Error - Use of Other Tables
    Given only compound_drug_analysis is specified for analysis
    When performing the analysis
    Then do not use other tables for enrichment or mapping

